WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.580
So how do you stay busy

2
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.960
after the launch?

3
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.660
Because a launch is a spike,

4
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.740
not a business.

5
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.760
Take Oriva.

6
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.120
Best launch week ever,

7
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.780
the founders answering messages

8
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.060
till two in the morning.

9
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.500
Three weeks later,

10
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.980
back where they started.

11
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.820
Now they want another launch.

12
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:36.760
Don’t.

13
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:37.620
That just buys

14
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.040
a second spike.

15
00:00:39.426 --> 00:00:41.226
So start with the fast part:

16
00:00:41.566 --> 00:00:42.486
paid media,

17
00:00:43.026 --> 00:00:43.446
ads judged

18
00:00:43.486 --> 00:00:44.366
by what one

19
00:00:44.406 --> 00:00:45.466
enquiry costs.

20
00:00:45.981 --> 00:00:47.101
The founders bet

21
00:00:47.141 --> 00:00:48.221
on LinkedIn.

22
00:00:48.261 --> 00:00:49.301
Café owners

23
00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:50.881
are business people, right?

24
00:00:51.101 --> 00:00:52.521
But for Oriva,

25
00:00:52.561 --> 00:00:53.421
an enquiry there

26
00:00:53.461 --> 00:00:54.461
costs five

27
00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:55.641
times Google.

28
00:00:56.061 --> 00:00:57.901
So the money moves to Google,

29
00:00:57.941 --> 00:00:59.481
and the ads follow people

30
00:00:59.521 --> 00:01:01.241
who already visited.

31
00:01:01.621 --> 00:01:02.961
Enquiries are back.

32
00:01:03.381 --> 00:01:04.481
But stop paying,

33
00:01:04.681 --> 00:01:06.001
and they stop too.

34
00:01:06.263 --> 00:01:07.983
Because ads are rented.

35
00:01:08.323 --> 00:01:09.823
Marketing is what you own:

36
00:01:10.223 --> 00:01:11.003
the steady work

37
00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:12.183
that keeps you found,

38
00:01:12.223 --> 00:01:13.283
every month.

39
00:01:13.543 --> 00:01:14.283
So Oriva

40
00:01:14.323 --> 00:01:15.383
writes a page

41
00:01:15.423 --> 00:01:16.483
for every search

42
00:01:16.523 --> 00:01:18.023
café owners type.

43
00:01:18.443 --> 00:01:20.023
And when one asks an AI

44
00:01:20.063 --> 00:01:21.183
for a roaster,

45
00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:22.783
Oriva starts to show up

46
00:01:22.823 --> 00:01:23.663
in the answer:

47
00:01:24.163 --> 00:01:25.583
roasted the week you order.

48
00:01:26.103 --> 00:01:26.923
Slower than ads,

49
00:01:27.203 --> 00:01:28.143
but it stacks.

50
00:01:28.743 --> 00:01:29.543
Still, being found

51
00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:30.803
isn’t being trusted.

52
00:01:31.169 --> 00:01:32.229
People trust customers

53
00:01:32.269 --> 00:01:33.589
more than brands.

54
00:01:33.629 --> 00:01:35.149
So we build a community:

55
00:01:35.469 --> 00:01:36.009
your buyers,

56
00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:37.269
talking to each other

57
00:01:37.309 --> 00:01:38.429
and to you.

58
00:01:39.026 --> 00:01:40.826
Oriva’s club lives on WhatsApp,

59
00:01:41.216 --> 00:01:41.956
where Malaysians

60
00:01:41.996 --> 00:01:43.256
actually are.

61
00:01:43.516 --> 00:01:44.636
Ambassadors bring friends,

62
00:01:44.676 --> 00:01:45.736
and earn

63
00:01:45.776 --> 00:01:46.876
free bags.

64
00:01:47.216 --> 00:01:48.456
With their okay,

65
00:01:48.496 --> 00:01:49.636
their photos become

66
00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.716
Oriva’s posts.

67
00:01:51.336 --> 00:01:52.306
Six months in,

68
00:01:52.346 --> 00:01:53.516
Oriva’s cheapest channel

69
00:01:53.556 --> 00:01:54.636
is its biggest.

70
00:01:55.056 --> 00:01:55.476
Great,

71
00:01:55.856 --> 00:01:57.556
until everyone starts messaging.

72
00:01:57.964 --> 00:01:59.184
So we bring in AI,

73
00:01:59.224 --> 00:02:00.704
doing real work

74
00:02:00.744 --> 00:02:02.424
under the brand’s rules.

75
00:02:02.864 --> 00:02:04.164
Remember launch week,

76
00:02:04.464 --> 00:02:06.044
answering till two in the morning?

77
00:02:06.464 --> 00:02:07.324
Now an AI

78
00:02:07.364 --> 00:02:08.384
assistant answers,

79
00:02:08.424 --> 00:02:09.504
in Oriva’s

80
00:02:09.544 --> 00:02:10.444
own words.

81
00:02:10.764 --> 00:02:12.404
It says it’s an AI.

82
00:02:12.764 --> 00:02:13.704
Three in the morning,

83
00:02:14.024 --> 00:02:15.524
a café in Penang asks

84
00:02:15.564 --> 00:02:17.364
if the Ethiopia’s in.

85
00:02:20.304 --> 00:02:20.984
The founders?

86
00:02:21.544 --> 00:02:22.084
Asleep.

87
00:02:22.404 --> 00:02:23.264
But replies aren’t

88
00:02:23.304 --> 00:02:24.484
the only busy work.

89
00:02:24.799 --> 00:02:25.699
Last piece:

90
00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:27.299
marketing automation.

91
00:02:27.719 --> 00:02:29.119
Your tools wired together,

92
00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:30.239
so routine

93
00:02:30.279 --> 00:02:31.699
work does itself.

94
00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:33.750
Posts schedule themselves.

95
00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:35.810
Every lead gets a score,

96
00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:36.950
and the hottest café

97
00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.750
goes to sales first.

98
00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:39.950
Every Monday,

99
00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.710
the numbers just arrive.

100
00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:43.010
Now look at this.

101
00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:44.390
Those numbers decide

102
00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.850
where next month’s

103
00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.110
ad money goes.

104
00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.370
So nothing goes back

105
00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.430
to where it started.

106
00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.171
So, more ads?

107
00:02:53.471 --> 00:02:54.651
Only where they pay.

108
00:02:55.031 --> 00:02:55.851
More posts?

109
00:02:56.331 --> 00:02:57.691
Your buyers make them.

110
00:02:57.971 --> 00:02:58.891
Another launch?

111
00:02:59.211 --> 00:03:00.731
You may never need one.

112
00:03:00.771 --> 00:03:02.251
Because growth isn’t how

113
00:03:02.291 --> 00:03:03.371
hard you push.

114
00:03:03.651 --> 00:03:04.651
It’s what keeps running

115
00:03:04.691 --> 00:03:06.331
when you stop pushing.

116
00:03:06.748 --> 00:03:08.148
That’s all six phases.

117
00:03:08.648 --> 00:03:09.468
So, what does it cost,

118
00:03:09.508 --> 00:03:11.108
and when is it done?

119
00:03:11.568 --> 00:03:14.100
That’s next.

